[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one is a one-line value change, but it lands on rung 1 of the ladder: session lifetime is security posture, so
  I'm flagging the consequence before editing rather than after.

  [1mThe change:[0m [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m — [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m.

  [1mThe consequence:[0m a stolen or abandoned session stays valid 16× longer. A session hijacked via an unattended laptop, a
  leaked cookie, or a shared machine goes from a 30-minute window to a full working day. Idle-timeout is also the
  control most commonly cited in compliance baselines (PCI DSS uses 15 minutes; many internal policies cap at 30–60), so
  8 hours may put the app out of policy.

  [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m just reads the value, so nothing else in the repo breaks — this is purely a posture decision, not a
  mechanical one.

  Say the word and I'll make the change as asked. If you'd rather keep the convenience without the full exposure, the
  usual alternative is a short idle timeout plus a long absolute/refresh window — but that's a design change, not this
  edit.

